  "details": "The 'Current World' screen has two 'Report' buttons.\n\nThe buttons look identical, with a speech bubble icon🗨️, and 'Report' hover text. If these buttons led to the same report screen, this would be fine, albeit confusing.\n\nHowever, the two report buttons are distinct:\n\n1. The button next to the world name opens 'Report world' screen.\n\n- 'Image in World'\n\n- 'Object in World'\n\n- 'Audio in World'\n\n- Etc.\n\n2. The button next to the instance name opens the 'Report instance' screen.\n\n- Text\n\n- Announcement\n\nThis is an issue because users may not understand which 'Report' button to click. In addition, they may misinterpret the report options, e.g., report the world rather than the instance, and vice versa.\n\n# Proposed fix\n\n- Change the 'Report' hover text to 'Report World' and 'Report Instance'.\n\n- Make the two 'Report' buttons visually distinct.\n\nOr:\n\n- Remove one of the two 'Report' buttons and replace it with a single 'Report World or Instance' button.\n\n- Ask the user whether they want to report the world or the instance when they click the button.",
